# Database: Drizzle ORM

All database interactions must use the Drizzle schema and query builder. Never use raw SQL strings or any other ORM/query library.

## Schema

Tables are defined in [src/db/schema.ts](mdc:src/db/schema.ts):

- `decksTable` — `id`, `clerkUserId`, `name`, `description`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`
- `cardsTable` — `id`, `deckId` (FK → decks), `front`, `back`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`

## DB Client

Import the db instance from [src/db/index.ts](mdc:src/db/index.ts):

```ts
import { db } from "@/db";
import { decksTable, cardsTable } from "@/db/schema";
```

## Querying

```ts
// ✅ GOOD — Drizzle query builder
const decks = await db.select().from(decksTable).where(eq(decksTable.clerkUserId, userId));

// ❌ BAD — raw SQL
const decks = await db.execute(sql`SELECT * FROM decks WHERE clerk_user_id = ${userId}`);
```

## Mutations

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
await db.insert(cardsTable).values({ deckId, front, back });
await db.update(decksTable).set({ name }).where(eq(decksTable.id, id));
await db.delete(cardsTable).where(eq(cardsTable.id, id));
```

## Relations

Use `with` for joined queries via the defined relations (`decksRelations`, `cardsRelations`):

```ts
const deckWithCards = await db.query.decksTable.findFirst({
  where: eq(decksTable.id, deckId),
  with: { cards: true },
});
```
